 ## Overview
-Focus+Context via Opacity Modulation is an interaction technique that modifies the compositing scheme to increase the transparency of flat, uninteresting regions while preserving local details in areas of interest [S1, unofficial]. It solves the problem of occlusion in volume rendering by allowing users to see internal structures without completely removing the surrounding context, which can cause disorientation [S2, book]. Unlike [Cropping](1648-cropping.md), which removes data entirely, this method retains a translucent representation of the context, and unlike [Focus+Context Visualization via Deformation](3001-focus-context-visualization-via-deformation.md), it does not distort the geometry [S1, unofficial].
