 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** Linear with respect to the number of samples per ray, similar to standard volume rendering, as it adds a constant-time modulation calculation per sample [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Memory Complexity:** No additional memory beyond standard volume rendering buffers, as modulation is computed on-the-fly [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Performance:** Performance impact is minimal, primarily dependent on the cost of shading calculations [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Strengths:** Preserves context without occlusion; intuitive for users to understand flat vs. detailed regions; no geometric distortion [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Limitations:** May not effectively hide complex, non-flat structures; relies on shading which can be ambiguous in noisy data [S1, unofficial].
-*   **When to Use:** When users need to see internal structures without losing the spatial context of the surrounding volume, especially in medical imaging or scientific visualization [S2, book].
-*   **When Not to Use:** When the volume has complex, non-flat structures that need to be hidden, or when shading is unreliable due to noise [S1, unofficial].
